data.content:
Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the template with `@typeparam TItem`, a `<ul>` loop rendering each item via `ItemTemplate`, and Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` code-behind:

- **Immutability**: `OnParametersSet` copies `Items` into a private `_items` list, so the parent's collection is never mutated.
- **Generic**: Works with any `TItem`.
- **Events**: `OnOrderChanged` fires an `EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<TItem>>` with the reordered copy after each swap.

Usage matches your example — just name the template `ItemTemplate`:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { /* ... */ };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
